Data
The soils with both Bruker and Thermo spectra, except those in excluded. The Bruker files end at 3997.5 cm⁻¹, so the grid stops at 3996 cm⁻¹. Both spectra of a soil are averaged over their replicates and interpolated onto the same grid:

pw = np.arange(650, 3997, 2)
ids = [i for i in sorted(set(bruker_files()) & set(spa_files()), key=int) if i not in excluded]
br, th = load_bruker(pw, ids), load_fuku(pw, ids)
test_eq(br.sample_ids, th.sample_ids)
len(ids), sum(int(i) &gt;= 2600 for i in ids)

(376, 316)



gas_bands = {'H₂O': [(1300, 2000), (3500, 3950)], 'CO₂': [(650, 720), (2280, 2390)]}
def shade(ax):
    for (gas, bands), color in zip(gas_bands.items(), ['tab:blue', 'tab:gray']):
        for lo, hi in bands: ax.axvspan(lo, hi, color=color, alpha=0.1, lw=0)
    ax.invert_xaxis(); ax.set_xlabel('Wavenumber (cm⁻¹)')
in_band = lambda lo, hi: (pw &gt;= lo) & (pw &lt;= hi)
regions = {'650–1300': in_band(650, 1300), 'H₂O 1300–2000': in_band(1300, 2000), 'CO₂ 2280–2390': in_band(2280, 2390), 'quiet 2400–2800': in_band(2400, 2800), '2800–3500': in_band(2800, 3500), 'H₂O 3500–3950': in_band(3500, 3950)}

Mean spectra
The mean raw and SNV spectra of each instrument, and the difference of the SNV means. The shaded regions are the water vapour (blue) and CO₂ (grey) bands:

snv = SNV()
S = {'Bruker': br.spectra, 'Thermo': th.spectra}
fig, axs = plt.subplots(3, 1, figsize=(9, 8), sharex=True)
for k, X in S.items():
    axs[0].plot(pw, X.mean(0), lw=0.8, label=k)
    axs[1].plot(pw, snv.transform(X).mean(0), lw=0.8, label=k)
axs[2].plot(pw, snv.transform(th.spectra).mean(0) - snv.transform(br.spectra).mean(0), lw=0.8, c='k')
for ax, t in zip(axs, ['Mean absorbance', 'Mean SNV', 'Thermo − Bruker (SNV)']): ax.set_ylabel(t); shade(ax)
axs[0].legend()
for ax in axs[:2]: ax.set_xlabel('')
{k: (round(float(X.mean()), 3), round(float(X.std(1).mean()), 3)) for k, X in S.items()}








{'Bruker': (1.918, 0.398), 'Thermo': (0.514, 0.066)}


The pair of numbers per instrument is the mean absorbance and the mean within-spectrum standard deviation.

Plotting
plot_params plots statistics of ParamStats against the epoch, one line per parameter whose label contains kind, plus the head weights. Each line is a rolling mean over smooth records, on a log scale:



plot_params
def plot_params(
    rec, # Record from `tracked_fit`
    stats:tuple=('update', 'grad', 'moved'), # Columns of `rec['params']` to plot, one panel each
    kind:str='conv', # Part of the parameter label to select, such as 'conv' or 'BN γ'
    smooth:int=10, # Window of the rolling mean, in records
):
Plot stats of each selected parameter over training



plot_params(rec_syn, smooth=1);








plot_acts plots the activation statistics of each block over training. The second row shows each block’s histogram over training, as fastai’s color_dim does: the colour is the log of the count, and the vertical axis spans activations from 0 to 10:



plot_acts
def plot_acts(
    rec, # Record from `tracked_fit`
):
Plot the mean, standard deviation, share ≤ 0.05 and histogram of each block’s activations over training



plot_acts(rec_syn);

Pretraining
The augmented model trains as the saved model ossl_kex_snv_d1 did: the same split, seed and schedule (20 epochs, learning rate 10⁻³). The last epoch, with the OSSL validation R²:

models = {'no augmentation': load_pretrained('ossl_kex_snv_d1'), 'augmentation': pretrain_aug(Xo, yo, 'ossl_kex_aug', SpectralAug())}
pretrain_history('ossl_kex_aug').iloc[-1].round(3).to_dict()

{'train_loss': 0.028, 'valid_loss': 0.032, 'r2_score': 0.782}

Data and features
Two targets: log1p of Kex in cmolc/kg, as in 03_kex, and the Cs137 study’s log10 ratio of exchangeable to total Cs-137, as in 10_cs137. Both are scored on these scales. The features, as in 10_cs137: the spectra after SNV and a Savitzky-Golay first derivative, and block 4 of the saved OSSL Kex model, of the OSSL Kex and CEC models together, and of a model with random weights as a control:

fuku = load_fuku()
ids = fuku.sample_ids
props = fuku.source.reindex(ids)
ref_dir = fuku_path()/'reference'
ratio = pd.concat([pd.read_csv(ref_dir/f'cs137_ratio_{s}.csv', usecols=['ID', 'exCs137_totalCs137']) for s in ('train', 'test')])
ratio = ratio.assign(ID=ratio.ID.astype(str)).set_index('ID')['exCs137_totalCs137']
targets = {'Kex': np.log1p(props['soil_ex_K2O'].to_numpy() / mg_k2o_per_cmolc), 'Cs-137 ratio': ratio.reindex(ids).to_numpy()}
{k: int(np.isfinite(v).sum()) for k, v in targets.items()}

{'Kex': 1388, 'Cs-137 ratio': 1389}


